From: Alex Hoffmann <alex@dotstartech.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Persist NXP config timestamp on /data

The applied-configuration stamp lives in /var/tmp which is tmpfs on
this image, so isNxpConfigModified() returns true on every boot and the
HAL re-runs the full one-time config-apply pass (with several 1s
command timeouts, adding tens of seconds to every NFC init). Store the
stamp on the persistent /data partition instead.

Signed-off-by: Alex Hoffmann <alex@dotstartech.com>
---
--- a/src/nfcandroid_nfc_hidlimpl/halimpl/utils/phNxpConfig.cpp
+++ b/src/nfcandroid_nfc_hidlimpl/halimpl/utils/phNxpConfig.cpp
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
 #define config_pn557      "pn557"
 #define IsStringValue       0x80000000
 
-const char config_timestamp_path[] = "/var/tmp/libnfc-nxp-stamp-h1";
+const char config_timestamp_path[] = "/data/libnfc-nxp-stamp-h1";
 
 using namespace::std;
 
